          "prp": "Parallel Redundancy Protocol (IEC 62439-3), on 20 frames, and DELIBERATELY not implemented - these 20 are the reference's own false positives and reproducing them would be theatre. Every one is a TCP-over-IPv6 segmentation-offload frame whose IPv6 Payload Length is 0, so the reference has no length telling it where the payload ends and scans for PRP-0's 4-byte trailer instead. It finds one in the middle of an encrypted TLS record (frame 8200: bytes 4b 99 b1 00 at offset 266, LAN nibble B, 12-bit size 256 = 266+4-14) because PRP-0's only self-check is that its own size field agrees with its own position. Twenty hits over 180k frames is about what 1-in-32768 predicts. Industrial ring redundancy does not run on a home browsing capture. If a real PRP capture ever lands in test/fixtures, implement it then and floor it against that - not against this."
